<!--
PRESENT-TENSE SEMANTIC STATE — REALIZATION R1.1

Identity
This is a standalone Three.js civilization, built from the supplied S2 contract and
reference evidence. Three.js 0.180.0 is embedded as data modules; opening the HTML does
not fetch a renderer, an image, or a font. The frozen S2 contract is retained below.
The historical empty-apparatus description is archaeology, not current application truth.

Owners and invariants
- `terrain` owns a mutable sampled heightfield, surface support and extraction. Removal
  lowers the actual rendered/collidable substrate. Removed volume becomes quantified
  material using seven inventory units per cubic terrain unit. There is a lower bedrock
  bound. Excavation does not replenish itself.
- `world.lots` owns every exposed, contained, carried, routed and ballistic material lot.
  Each lot has quantity by four mineral/aggregate constituents, stage, location/owner,
  and a set of origin witnesses. A split partitions quantity; combination sums it;
  separation preserves it. No productive cooldown creates material.
- Initial inventory + extracted terrain = all extant matter. The ledger reports the
  residual. Runtime conservation failure stops execution visibly.
- Inventory, reserved incoming cargo, capacity and compatible processing stages govern
  acceptance. Materials cannot silently arrive in a full container. Scheduling checks
  other eligible loads when the first load is blocked.
- Collector delivery and ring freight are separate layers. Newly collected world matter enters
  the civilization through Unzip's explicit intake capability; drones do not deposit into generic
  buffers or downstream consumers merely because they have room.
- One transport graph belongs to the world. Cities expose interfaces, not pairwise
  knowledge. Ring freight is hub-mediated: every inter-city freight journey passes through
  Link City. Processing/storage endpoints never connect directly to one another. Dijkstra
  still resolves currently available paths, but Link is now required infrastructure rather
  than an optional express shortcut.
  Disabling a link causes later loads to seek alternate paths. In-flight loads return
  to an available adjacent interface, or spill and fall if neither endpoint remains.
  Terrain clearance, endpoint power, interface availability and link state affect routes.
- Physics owns gravitational settling for loose lots, launched loads and whole cities.
  A city rests on the highest of eight footing samples. It does not tilt or fracture.
  Powered drone flight and ring transport explicitly supply lift. Support is resampled.
- The observer owns camera, pause/speed and investigation interventions. Selection does
  not move the camera. Relocation moves a container and its contents; spatial reach changes route
  availability. Existing cargo recovers along its current edge instead of teleporting
  when an endpoint moves. Recovery also respects receiving capacity. An undercut is actual terrain extraction and tests support, not an animation.

Capabilities
Launcher: held packaged material is committed to a ballistic delivery. The rotating
accelerator's muzzle is the launch origin; elevation is solved from the same gravity
and flight time as the projectile. It chooses a relatively undersupplied marked ground.
Landed cargo becomes recoverable raw material with the original constituent amounts.
There is no combat model and no resource sink disguised as a delivery.
Drone: twenty-four maintained collectors claim exposed lots, fly to them, lift actual
cargo and choose available receiving capabilities. Held cargo stays attached to its drone.
Collection and receiving capacity are finite. Drones wait when no work or receiver exists.
Unzip: raw lots are separated into single-constituent lots, shown in four corresponding
architectural output bins. Their stored identity drives the classification and colors.
Thumper: available exposed stock regulates excavation. Its swept supported arm and
reciprocating head act at the same world location as the terrain cut. Work sites progress
within its reachable annulus; bedrock and accumulated stock can stop productive work.
Reservoir: retains constituent amounts and origin witnesses. Its visible fill is a persistent
spatial witness rather than a frame-by-frame repacking: inventory deltas accrete into
strata inside the actual hemispherical containment envelope, and withdrawals peel the
newest compatible visible strata first. Internal sorted-to-packed Zip changes packaging
without spatially shuffling unchanged stored composition. A packaging operation combines
sorted inputs into mixed recoverable loads. Brass capsule bands communicate coherent
packaging; nothing is homogenized away.
Link: fast relay interfaces change least-cost paths between freight-participating cities.
It can fail or be isolated, but it is transit infrastructure rather than a warehouse; cargo
may wait at its interface while traversing a route but does not become Link inventory.
Drone City and Thumper expose no ring-freight interfaces and own no authoritative material
storage. Drone cargo is delivered to actual receiving/processing capabilities; Thumper output
exists directly as exposed world-space matter. Cityhood itself grants neither storage nor
freight connectivity.

Representation and extension boundaries
Cities have distinct verb-derived masses: directional bastions, porous fabrication bays,
branching separator, heavy gantry, hollow containment ring, sparse relay spires. Brass,
stone, selected glass, repeated octagons and rectilinear urban density unify them.
Static architecture is merged by material within each movable city; trees, buildings,
ring teeth and matter use instancing. Each bead is a sample of an authoritative lot,
not an independent rigid body or a promise of a one-bead-to-one-unit ratio. The visible
reservoir fill derives from inventory through a persistent bounded presentation history;
it does not create authoritative matter. Moving beads derive from extant cargo only.
The matter presentation budget is bounded. The simulation runs at a fixed 30 Hz step.
No ecosystem, civilian population or internal building economy is implied by greeble.
Material origin witnesses are sets, not an exact per-origin mass ledger; constituent
quantities are exact. Forests and decorative rocks are scenery, not collectible stock.
The finite surface lots and extracted substrate are the collectible world substance.
Water and vegetation are scenic approximations; no hydrology, tree collision or erosion
simulation is claimed. Drone steering enforces terrain clearance but not full obstacle
pathfinding. Cities are atomic supported bodies rather than simulated district structures.
The session starts from a deterministic seed when reopened; there is no persistent save.

To extend the world, add a capability that consumes/produces existing lots or introduce
an explicit new world truth. New consumers should declare compatibility and capacity;
new terrain causes should call terrain.extract; new vehicles should transfer ownership
rather than changing counters. Update the audit if a genuine transformation introduces
a new stored/consumed material account. Geometry and labels do not establish a capability.

ARCHAEOLOGY / LEARNED EVIDENCE
- A blocked first eligible lot originally starved other ready cargo. Scheduling now
  searches eligible outgoing lots; this is a logistics rule, not a named-city exception.
- Arrival-only capacity checks were insufficient with multiple concurrent carriers.
  Incoming reservations now participate in acceptance and drone receiver choice.
- A visually aimed accelerator can disagree with a correct projectile solver. Muzzle
  position, elevation and ballistic velocity now share the same world-space solution.
- Unrestricted raw intake could deadlock a full Reservoir against a full separator.
  Raw intake now has a bounded staging allowance; processed stock retains the space
  needed to resume circulation after an interruption.
- Bare shortest-distance routing left fast infrastructure unused. Relay speed now enters
  both path cost and actual flight time; Link's benefit is measurable rather than decorative.
- About 1,000 first-pass draw calls were unnecessary. Static geometry merging and instanced
  ring teeth reduced submission cost without removing the machines or material populations.
- Human inspection of a nearly full Reservoir exposed a presentation scar: cylindrical
  fill clipped through the hemispherical glass and frame-by-frame inventory traversal made
  stored matter appear to churn. The fill witness now conforms to the dome and preserves
  spatial history. This changed presentation ownership, not conserved inventory semantics.
- R1.2.2 tested a compact 1.15–2.25 second Launcher flight regime after human inspection
  found the original ballistic delivery perceptually slow. The projectile remained under
  unchanged 9.8 world gravity, but compressing flight time made the accelerator nearly
  horizontal and collapsed its ballistic silhouette. The probe was informative but rejected.
  R1.2.3 restores the prior time-based ballistic solver exactly; no interpolation or trail
  is added. The unresolved kinetic-readability problem remains explicit rather than hiding
  it behind a failed tuning change.
- The original realization autonomously fired packaged matter at three reclamation grounds
  to close the conserved material loop. Human inspection exposed that this circulation was
  mechanically coherent but did not establish an earned civilization-level reason to fire.
  R1.2.3 withdraws autonomous launch demand. Launcher now waits with packaged supply until
  the observer presses LAUNCH; that commitment provisionally selects one reclamation ground
  at random, the machine aims, and the existing ballistic consequence proceeds normally.
  Reclamation grounds remain experimental scaffolding, not asserted world demand.
- R1.3.14 deliberately removes Unzip as the civilization throughput governor. Human inspection
  found that its visible verb already reads correctly, while its old 150-unit / 2.1s processing
  gate and generic 1.5s export cadence made the whole simulation wait on the separator. Unzip now
  processes up to 360 raw units every 0.35 simulation seconds and receives a 0.28s forwarding
  cadence while preserving differentiated stock, four visible embedded stock/ring witnesses,
  one serialized freight output, conserved lots, and ordinary Link transport constraints. This is
  experiential tuning: Unzip expresses processing but does not own civilization rhythm.
- R1.3.14 also relocates the western forest reclamation witness to the far arid coastal corner
  at (122,112). Ballistic target semantics are otherwise unchanged.
- The original supplied S2 empty apparatus follows as a frozen requirement/reference,
  along with the current executable. There is no recovered predecessor implementation.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.1 / RESERVOIR CONTAINMENT
Observation: human inspection after isolating Launcher filled Reservoir to 6,499 / 6,500
and made two presentation failures legible: matter crossed the dome boundary, and stored
matter globally shuffled despite no corresponding authoritative movement.
Interpretation: inventory truth was sound; its spatial witness was not. Storage should
retain visible history, and containment geometry should constrain presentation.
Intervention: preserve authoritative lots and Zip semantics; add a Reservoir-owned
presentation history derived only from inventory composition deltas. New composition
accretes at the exposed surface; withdrawals remove newest compatible visible material.
The fixed slot field occupies the actual ellipsoidal hemisphere, so full storage remains
inside glass. Internal packaging with unchanged composition causes no visual rearrangement.
Validation boundary: this is a presentation witness, not granular rigid-body simulation
or a new inventory stack rule. Conservation remains owned by world.lots and audit().

ARCHAEOLOGY ADDENDUM — R1.2 / TRANSPORT EXTENT + HALF-DUPLEX CONDUITS
- R1/R1.1 represented each conserved in-transit lot as one authoritative route point with
  a compact cloud of sampled beads. Quantity and composition were truthful, but distance
  collapsed perceptually into moving noise.
- The compact witness also concealed a simulation abstraction: opposing packets could
  occupy the same conduit simultaneously and pass through one another.
- R1.2 preserves lot identity, route choice, nominal edge velocity, capacity, conservation,
  and arrival semantics. It changes how occupied distance is witnessed and adds only the
  exclusion needed once that occupied distance becomes visible.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.2 / ELASTIC TRANSPORT
Observation: the human wanted streams to read as slower and more discrete over distance
without slowing the simulation. Ring conduits are arcs, so matter must inhabit those arcs
rather than straight noisy chords. Once spatial extent was made explicit, two opposing
packets crossing inside one conduit became a visible physical contradiction.
Interpretation: distance can be made legible through elastic spatial extent rather than
latency. Spatial extent creates minimal exclusion: a conduit is bidirectional while idle
but temporarily one-way while occupied.
Intervention: keep authoritative packet timing unchanged. Sampled matter now stretches
along routePoint() with maximum extent near mid-route and condenses at both interfaces.
Transverse jitter is small and route-local. Conduits admit same-direction followers only
after a small world-space headway; opposing packets wait compactly at interfaces until the
edge drains. Temporary traffic does not alter Dijkstra topology or trigger rerouting.
Validation boundary: this is not collision physics, congestion-aware routing, fairness,
or a general reservation framework. Continuous same-direction traffic may starve the
opposite direction; that remains observable evidence rather than a pre-solved policy.

PRESENT-TENSE TRANSPORT TRUTH — R1.2
A transported lot remains one conserved authoritative packet following its chosen path.
Its visible matter has route-conforming elastic extent: compact at departure and arrival,
most spatially discrete around mid-route. Conduit occupancy is half-duplex. Same-direction
packets may follow with minimum entry headway; opposing entry waits at the interface until
the conduit is free. Occupancy is traffic, not connectivity failure.

COLLABORATIVE PROBE — R1.2.5 / BALLISTIC TEMPORAL SCALE
The spatial arc and physical aiming are accepted evidence; projectile traversal remains too slow.
A temporary observer control cycles 1×, 1.5×, 2×, 2.5× and 3× ballistic temporal scale.
For a multiplier m, launch velocity is multiplied by m and projectile-only gravity by m²,
preserving the same integrated spatial parabola while changing traversal time. This is an
inspection probe, not yet promoted civilization truth. World gravity remains unchanged.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.2.4 / PHYSICAL AIMING
Observation: random manual targets exposed an aiming discontinuity. Yaw already traversed at
finite angular speed, while the ballistic elevation solver directly assigned visible barrel
pitch each simulation step, making the accelerator snap vertically between firing solutions.
Interpretation: numerical solution and machine actuation had accidentally become the same
operation. A physical accelerator should receive a desired firing orientation, then traverse
both axes before it can commit a shot.
Intervention: preserve the R1.2.3 ballistic timing, 9.8 world gravity, projectile integration,
and random observer-selected reclamation targets. The ballistic solver now returns a desired
pitch without leaving its temporary numerical samples on visible machinery. Yaw retains its
0.55 rad/s slew; pitch now has an independent bounded 0.42 rad/s slew. A committed launch
waits until both axes are aligned as well as packaged supply being present.
Validation boundary: this does not repair the known slow ballistic flight, change target
meaning, add interpolation, or introduce a general actuator framework. It only makes the
existing two-axis Launcher physically continuous and separates solution from actuation.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.2.3 / MANUAL LAUNCH + BALLISTIC REVERT
Observation: shortening Launcher flight time made firing faster but flattened the accelerator
and exposed a deeper question: the three reclamation targets existed mainly to keep matter
circulating, while drones serviced them without an independently earned demand.
Interpretation: ballistic tuning and launch purpose are separate questions. A failed kinetic
probe should be reverted rather than patched cosmetically, and provisional test destinations
should not silently become autonomous civilization intent.
Intervention: restore R1.2.1 ballistic timing and world gravity unchanged. Remove autonomous
fire. Add one observer LAUNCH affordance above the World ledger. It is available only with
at least one standard 75-unit packed shot; pressing it chooses one provisional reclamation
ground randomly, then the existing accelerator aim and physical launch resolve normally.
Validation boundary: this is not a targeting UI, demand model, launcher cooldown redesign,
or new ballistic solution. The observer exercises an existing capability while destination
meaning and kinetic readability remain open empirical questions.

SUCCESS-CONDITION REVIEW / EXECUTABLE EVIDENCE
1–2. Desktop and portrait renders expose six different function-derived silhouettes,
     unified by brass/stone, octagonal details, partial glass and urban density.
3. Excavation changes the heightfield; an undercut test lowered a city's supported
   elevation by roughly 1.7 world units rather than leaving it suspended.
4–5. Exact constituent amounts survive every transfer. The running test contained both
     mixed packaged cargo and single-constituent sorted lots. Zip changes packaging,
     not constituent identity; launched mixed loads can be collected and separated again.
6–7. All displayed cargo samples extant lots. Disabling the direct collection-to-sorter
     edge changed its path to a route through Link. Unsupported interrupted cargo spills.
8–9. Running counters and owned state show extraction, drone collection, separation,
     packaging, relay movement and ballistic delivery composing in one shared world.
10. Tests cover route interruption, isolation, supply exhaustion, reconnection and
    changed terrain support. Capacity bounds and nonnegative amounts remain intact.
11. A twenty-minute perturbation run continued circulating matter after recovery.
    A separate twenty-eight-minute sequence filled the Reservoir to within two units
    of its 6,500-unit limit, exhausted disconnected launch supply, and then drained
    the buffer and restarted deliveries after reconnection.
12. Desktop and 390×844 portrait layouts were rendered and inspected. Controls fit;
