    frame used 162 draw calls versus about 1,000 in the first pass. Bead sampling adapts
    to the whole population rather than hiding later lots when a budget is reached.
    Headless Chromium validation is not a hardware frame-rate guarantee for every phone.
14–15. This semantic state, the original S2 contract, named state owners, inspection API
       and archaeological findings accompany the executable. Renderer vendor bytes are
       isolated at the end of the HTML so the civilization source remains readable.
16. Buffering, starvation, alternate routing, settling and recovery are measured
    consequences of shared state, not a timeline of six pre-authored demonstrations.

Conservation during the long tests remained within approximately 10^-10 units, including
separate audits for all four constituents. Browser tests reported no page/runtime errors.
No physical mobile device was available for validation. There is no claim of individually
simulated bearings, fluid dynamics, general rigid-body contact or strategic city planning.




R1.3.2 ARCHAEOLOGY — COLLECTION NEEDS AN INTAKE, NOT A NEAREST BUFFER

Observation: after freight topology became truthful, collector drones could still choose among
multiple cities that happened to accept raw cargo. In practice this let collection bypass the
processing story and made Reservoir behave like an alternate raw-material intake.
Interpretation: collection and freight acceptance are different capabilities. A drone carrying
newly exposed world matter should not infer a destination from spare capacity or generic buffering.
Intervention: Unzip now explicitly owns the civilization's current `intake` capability. Collector
drones deliver raw cargo only to an enabled intake with available capacity. Reservoir and Launcher
are downstream freight endpoints, not collection destinations. No additional consumer or processing
economy is invented by this correction.
Expected evidence: every collected ground lot enters Unzip first. If Unzip is disabled or full,
loaded drones hold cargo rather than bypassing it. Once accepted, material may proceed through the
existing Link-mediated logistics chain according to its transformed stage.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.3.2 / UNZIP AS COLLECTION INTAKE
Observation → drones were still able to shortcut the semantic pipeline at delivery.
Interpretation → the civilization needs an explicit boundary between world collection and ring
logistics.
Intervention → add an intake capability to Unzip and make drone receiver choice depend on intake,
not generic buffer/sort acceptance.
Validation target → ground → drone → Unzip is the only current collection path; a blocked Unzip
creates visible loaded-drone backpressure instead of rerouting raw cargo to Reservoir or Launcher.

R1.3.5 ARCHAEOLOGY — REJECTED APPROACH-GEOMETRY PATCH

Observation: particular claimed deposits left their assigned drone hovering/wobbling over the
material forever without pickup. R1.3.5 hypothesized that the cruise-to-descent transition was the
cause and changed that transition to horizontal proximity.
Result: the same deterministic deposits still failed. The intervention did not address the failure
and is withdrawn rather than accumulated as architecture. Temporary DRONES diagnostics were also
removed and remain absent.
Lesson: the drone had already done the semantically important work — it owned an exclusive claim and
had visibly reached the claimed patch. Requiring the generic movement helper to report exact arrival
was an unnecessarily strict condition for collection in this data-stream visualization.

R1.3.6 ARCHAEOLOGY — CLAIM PROXIMITY COMPLETES COLLECTION

Observation: broken collectors visibly hovered over their claimed material patches but pickup was
executed only when `moveToward()` reported exact arrival at the lot's mathematical pickup point.
Interpretation: navigation completion and material collection are separate concerns. Ground matter
is an aggregated stream witness with a visible footprint, not a precision docking socket. A drone
that exclusively owns the claim and has reached that patch has satisfied the collection contract.
Intervention: restore the pre-R1.3.5 crude approach behavior. Collection now completes when the
claiming drone is within 3.5 world units horizontally of the authoritative lot position. Exact
`moveToward()` completion no longer gates transfer. Claims, 45-unit cargo capacity, conservation,
and the world → drone → Unzip boundary are unchanged. No retries, expiry, pathfinding, terrain
special cases, or additional pile physics are introduced.
Validation target: the previously deterministic bad piles, including Thumper-side deposits, are
picked up once their claimant reaches the visible patch; ordinary distant flight remains unchanged.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.3.6 / LET CLAIMS COLLECT
Observation → drones visibly reached and hovered over claimed material yet exact navigation arrival
prevented transfer.
Interpretation → for this stream visualization, ownership plus local proximity is the meaningful
pickup condition; mathematical docking is not.
Intervention → decouple pickup from `moveToward()` return value and withdraw the failed R1.3.5
approach patch.
Validation target → no permanent claimed piles under hovering drones; no change to material routing,
capacity, conservation, or downstream processing.

Present truth after R1.3.6: a collector exclusively claims exposed ground matter, approaches it with
the original crude terrain-clearance flight, and collects once it reaches the claimed patch; newly
collected world matter enters the civilization through Unzip.

R1.3.15 PRESENT TRUTH — LINK OWNS ALLOCATION

Observation: Launcher could sit depleted while Reservoir remained half full. That contradicted the
intended civilization grammar: Reservoir is overflow, not a mandatory upstream supplier, and no
processing/storage city should decide allocation priority.
Interpretation: destination choice had accidentally lived in generic source dispatch. Link City is
the switchyard and therefore owns the allocation policy. Launcher always has first claim on usable
processed material; Reservoir receives overflow when Launcher cannot accept more. Stored Reservoir
material may re-enter Link allocation when Launcher has room.
Intervention: processed sorted or packed freight is allocated Launcher-first, Reservoir-second.
Launcher can consume processed sorted or packed stock; launch still forms one conserved 75-unit
packed projectile at commitment. Reservoir sorted stock is eligible to leave when Launcher has
headroom instead of being trapped as local processing input. All freight still traverses Link.
This is deliberate priority, not fill-ratio fairness.

R1.3.1 ARCHAEOLOGY — LINK MUST ACTUALLY BE THE NETWORK

Observation: after removing freight interfaces from Drone and Thumper, remaining freight
endpoints could still route directly to one another. Link was therefore an optional shortcut
rather than necessary transport infrastructure.
Interpretation: access to ring freight had been conflated with permission to create peer-to-peer
conduits. That weakened Link's verb and produced visually noisy, semantically redundant routes.
Intervention: route construction now creates only endpoint-to-Link spokes. Every inter-city
ring journey is hub-mediated. Link owns no ordinary inventory; material may occupy its interface
while waiting for an outbound conduit without becoming Link stock. Existing half-duplex traffic,
headway, waiting, fairness, interruption and conservation semantics remain intact.
Expected evidence: isolating Link halts all ring freight; Unzip accumulates output, Reservoir can
continue only from material already held, and Launcher eventually starves. No direct bypass route
appears.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.3.1 / REQUIRED LINK HUB
Observation → direct endpoint routes made Link optional and added ring spaghetti.
Interpretation → a freight interface means access to a network, not peer-to-peer connectivity.
Intervention → star topology centered on Link; no endpoint-to-endpoint ring routes.
Validation target → all freight paths between distinct processing/storage cities contain Link,
and disabling Link visibly partitions the entire ring logistics layer.

Present truth after R1.3.1: Link City is required mediation for inter-city ring freight.

R1.3 ARCHAEOLOGY — CITYHOOD IS NOT A FREIGHT INTERFACE
R1 generated ring routes from spatial proximity between every city and gave every city a
capacity. Inspection showed that this generic-city abstraction produced false semantics:
Drone City accumulated raw material in a buffer with no downstream purpose; Thumper exposed
matter directly into world space yet still advertised storage and ring connectivity; Link
advertised warehouse capacity despite normal operation never placing material there and no
legible storage volume existing in its morphology. These were not repaired by inventing
maintenance economies or pairwise route exceptions. The overgeneralization was withdrawn.

Present truth after R1.3: freight interfaces are explicit capabilities. Launcher, Unzip,
Reservoir and Link participate in the ring network because their current verbs require it.
Drone City and Thumper do not. Authoritative city inventory exists only where material
genuinely resides as part of a simulated verb. Link relays transit without owning ordinary
warehouse inventory. Interrupted cargo may recover only into an endpoint that actually has
storage; otherwise existing retreat/spill behavior remains the physical consequence.

COLLABORATIVE TURN RECORD — R1.3 / MATERIAL + NETWORK ONTOLOGY
Observation: visually nonsensical ring connections existed; Drone City filled and remained
full; Link and Thumper exposed capacities unsupported by their behavior or morphology.
Interpretation: a generic city abstraction had silently conferred storage and freight
connectivity on entities whose verbs did not earn either capability.
Intervention: removed Drone/Thumper freight participation and generic capacity, removed Link
warehouse capacity, restricted route construction to explicit freight interfaces, and made
inspection UI distinguish transit-only/no-inventory cities from actual containers.
Validation target: Drone and Thumper have no ring routes; Link still changes network topology
without accumulating inventory; drones deliver collected raw matter only to genuine receiving
capabilities; Unzip/Reservoir/Launcher retain bounded material state; conservation and existing
transport behavior remain intact.


FORWARD ROADMAP — POST-R1.2.5 / LEGIBILITY + OWNERSHIP PASS
This is working intent, not present-tense civilization truth. Execute in order because each
step should expose evidence for the next. Do not preserve an implementation merely because
it already exists. Do not broaden scope unless observation earns it.

1. MATERIAL / NETWORK ONTOLOGY
Correct the generic-city overgeneralization before aesthetic cleanup. Cityhood does not
confer storage, material ownership, or freight connectivity. Capacity and connectivity are
independent capabilities earned by function. Drone City and Thumper should not participate
in ring freight merely because they are cities. Link remains transport infrastructure but
does not need ordinary warehouse inventory. Preserve authoritative inventories only where
matter genuinely resides or waits as part of the verb: Unzip processing, Reservoir storage,
and Launcher feed/readiness. Remove nonsensical routes as a consequence of truthful
interfaces rather than by pairwise exceptions.

Observed scar motivating this pass: Drone City currently fills a generic buffer and then
remains full; Link exposes capacity it does not normally use and has no legible safe storage
volume; Thumper owns capacity despite exposing matter directly into world space. Plausible
maintenance economies (drone repair, machine consumables, etc.) are intentionally outside
this lab until they earn relevance. The authoritative material simulation tracks material
whose movement/transformation matters to this experiment, not every material requirement
of the implied civilization.

2. DRONE LEGIBILITY
Keep the existing collection semantics small. Remove misleading reclamation-target witness
geometry when that scaffolding is retired. Repair the stereotyped diagonal/fixed-angle flight
read so drone orientation and approach communicate actual travel and pickup. Collection is
arrival at exposed ground matter, not an invented harvesting timer. Do not add repair
economics, elaborate pathfinding, or flocking unless evidence requires them.

3. LAUNCHER DISPERSAL PROBE
Preserve the accepted physical two-axis aiming behavior. Retire the temporary SHOT temporal
probe and continuous coherent ballistic flight. Test Launcher as redistribution by dispersal:
a coherent packed load is committed, the machine deliberately aims, discharge converts that
load into spatially distributed raw ground matter, and particulate rain creates a broad
recoverable field for drones. Conservation and composition remain exact. Packaging is
destroyed by dispersal. Distribution footprint should have real downstream collection
consequences. Provisional reclamation bullseyes are scaffolding, not earned civilization
demand.

4. VISUAL HIERARCHY
Only after topology is truthful, tune perceptual hierarchy. Let city structural mass separate
from terrain/ecology; reserve brighter brass/gold emphasis for machinery, interfaces, and
meaningful network activity. Matter must remain visibly distinct. Prefer active routes to
assert themselves over inactive infrastructure. Do not clear forests or delete environmental
density merely to solve palette/attention collisions. Reassess ring count after meaningless
routes disappear before making additional reductions.

5. TWO-MINUTE LEGIBILITY PASS
Inspect from a fresh start as a first-time viewer rather than a developer. The artifact should
be attractive immediately, yield a crude causal model within roughly a minute, and allow one
or two genuine interventions to reveal backpressure, transport, processing, storage, or
redistribution within roughly two minutes. Keep controls as real interventions rather than
scripted demo buttons. World Ledger remains a deeper inspection hatch. Prefer revelation of
existing depth over adding systems.

6. THUMPER — LAST SUBSTANTIAL EXPEDITION
Do not redesign Thumper during earlier cleanup. Preserve the earned truth that extraction is
local, persistent, and visibly depletes/scars one bounded place. Later replace the oversized
stamp/boom morphology with a stationary radial excavation works: lateral reach larger than
the city footprint, progressive substrate removal around the installation, an ever-deepening
local pit, and city descent as supporting terrain is removed. Excavated matter remains
ordinary world-space collectible matter. Reconsider the current global loose-stock throttle
in the context of the local worksite rather than patching it prematurely.

STOP CONDITION
