- accepts compatible supplied matter or payloads whose relevant identity exists in
  authoritative world state;
- supplied matter does not simply vanish into an unrelated cooldown;
- converts or commits supplied matter into a launched physical/logistical consequence;
- can launch toward a meaningful world-space destination, target, route, or transport
  interface;
- lack of supply should matter;
- launch origin and direction should be visually causal;
- its defense/logistics behavior should be capable of interacting with world conditions
  rather than existing solely as a looping animation.

The implementation may introduce targets, threats, deliveries, construction payloads, or
other uses if they strengthen composition. Do not let "defense" force the entire world
into a combat game.


2. DRONE CITY — FABRICATION + COLLECTION

Identity:
A dense fabrication city with distributed launch bays and an autonomous working swarm.

Required morphology:
- shared civilization base language;
- especially dense vertical urban interior;
- multiple visible launch / recovery bays or distributed drone interfaces;
- visible drone population at a scale sufficient to read as a swarm without overwhelming
  performance;
- storage or staging areas that visibly respond to returned material.

Required semantics:
- fabricates, releases, or otherwise maintains autonomous collector drones;
- drones perceive or discover available collectable matter through world state;
- drones travel through world space;
- collection requires reaching or otherwise meaningfully interacting with matter;
- collected matter becomes carried/owned cargo rather than disappearing globally;
- drones return or deliver cargo to a compatible receiving capability;
- returned material changes visible/authoritative storage or flow;
- drones should not contain special-case knowledge of a particular Thumper, Reservoir, or
  named destination when shared capability semantics can suffice.

