Identity:
A processing city whose architecture visibly turns incoming mixed flow into separated
outgoing flows.

Required morphology:
- shared octagonal brass/stone/glass civilization language;
- one or more prominent receiving interfaces;
- multiple outgoing interfaces / ring berths;
- a visible processing volume or machinery zone;
- separated output streams should be visually distinguishable by the material identity
  the realization has established.

Required semantics:
- receives matter from compatible incoming transport or delivery;
- can accept mixed populations;
- classifies or separates according to material distinctions that genuinely exist in
  authoritative world state; provenance may be one such distinction when consequential;
- maintains quantity through sorting except for explicit, legible loss/transformation;
- produces multiple usable outgoing populations/streams;
- downstream consumers are chosen by compatibility/network state rather than because the
  sorter knows six predetermined scene scripts;
- processing state should be visible enough to understand that sorting is occurring.

"Unzip" is a semantic metaphor for one mixed stream becoming several differentiated
flows. The exact machinery is implementation-owned.


